   \[
   \text{Concentration} = \frac{0.044 \text{ g}}{100 \text{ mL}} = 0.00044 \text{ g/mL}
   \]

2. **Calculate the mass of sodium fluoride in 10 mL:**
   \[
   \text{Mass} = \text{Concentration} \times \text{Volume} = 0.00044 \text{ g/mL} \times 10 \text{ mL} = 0.0044 \text{ g}
   \]

3. **Convert the mass from grams to milligrams:**
