2. **Mechanism**: The inhibition is attributed to the presence of **phyto-inositol-1-inositol-2-phosphate (PIP)** analogs in the extract. These compounds are structurally analogs of inositol pyrophosphate (IPP), which are known to inhibit PKA by binding to its regulatory subunit (PKA2R).  
