The most common type of mutation is a **miss-sense mutation**, where a single amino acid is replaced in the COLP1 gene, leading to a non-functional or dysfunctional COLP1 protein. This defect in the COLP1 protein leads to abnormal collagen structure and integrity, which causes the symptoms of Marfan syndrome.

