- $f(16) > 3$
- $f(32) > \frac{7}{2}$

The general form is $f(2^n) > \frac{n+1}{2}$. 

For $n = 2$, $f(2) = \frac{3}{2} > \frac{2+1}{2} = \frac{3}{2}$.
