**1. Definition of the Riemann-Liouville Fractional Derivative**
The Riemann-Liouville fractional derivative \( aD_t^p f(t) \) is defined as:
\[
aD_t^p f(t) = \frac{a}{t^{p+1}} \int_a^t (t - t')^p f(t') \, dt',
\]
where \( p > 0 \) and \( a > 0 \).

