2. **Negate the proposition**: The negation of "" If \( p \), then \( q \)"" is "" \( p \) and \( \overline{q} \),"" where \( \overline{q} \) is the negation of \( q \).

3. **Negulate \( q \)**: The negation of "" \( A \cap B = B \)"" is \( \overline{q} \) = "" \( A \cap B \neq B \)."".

4. **Combine \( p \) and \( \overline{q} \)**: The negation of the given proposition is "" \( A \cup B = A \) and \( A \cap B \neq B \)."".

