   \]

3. **Calculate the Reynolds number (Re):**
   \[
   Re = \frac{\mu v d}{\mu_f}
   \]
   For water at 20°C, the kinematic viscosity is \(\mu_f = 1.0 \times 10^{-6} \text{ m}^2/\text{s}\).
   \[
   Re = \frac{(1.0 \times 10^{-6} \text{ m}^2/\text{s})(1.5 \text{ m/s})(0.04 \text{ m})}{1.0 \times 10^{-6} \text{ m}^2/\text{s}} = 0.06
