","To calculate the average radiation dose to the liver, we need to convert the energy absorbed to a dose unit (e.g., Gray or Gray equivalent). The gray (Gy) is the standard unit for radiation dose, defined as energy per unit mass. The gray equivalent (Gy/Gy) is a measure of the biological effect of radiation, which depends on the type of radiation.

