","(a) The acceleration of the proton is given by the formula:  
\[
a = \frac{qE}{m}
\]  
where \(q = 1.60 \times 10^{-19} \, \text{C}\) is the charge of the proton, \(E = 500 \, \text{N/C}\) is the electric field strength, and \(m = 1.67 \times 10^{-27} \, \text{kg}\) is the mass of the proton. Substituting the values:  
\[
a = \frac{(1.60 \times 10^{-19} \, \text{C})(500 \, \text{N/C})}{1.67 \times 10^{-27} \, \text{kg}} = 4.8 \times 10^{8} \, \text{m/s}^2
\]  
The magnitude of the acceleration is \(\boxed{4.8 \times 10^8 \, \text{m/s}^2}\).  

(b) The time it takes for the proton to reach a speed of \(35,000 \, \text{m/s}\) is given by the kinematic equation:  
\[
v = at
\]  
