   \[
   m_{\text{Earth}} \times v_{\text{Earth,final}} + m_{\text{cannon}} \times v_{\text{cannon,final}} = 0
   \]
   Here, \( v_{\text{Earth,final}} \) is the recoil velocity of the Earth, and \( v_{\text{cannon,final}} \) is the velocity of the cannonball after firing.

3. **Momentum conservation:**
   The total momentum before and after the collision must be equal:
   \[
   m_{\text{cannon}} \times v_{\text{cannon}} = m_{\text{Earth}} \times v_{\text{Earth,final}} + m_{\text{cannon}} \times v_{\text{cannon,final}}
   \]
