A simply supported beam of rectangular cross-section has a constant width \( b \) and a variable depth \( h \). The beam is subjected to a concentrated load \( F \) at a distance \( c \) from the right support. To ensure the maximum shear stress \( \tau_{\text{max}} \) due to direct shear is constant in the region where the depth \( h \) approaches zero, show that the depth \( h \) at location \( x \) (measured from the left support) is given by:  
\[
h = \frac{3}{2} \frac{Fc}{lb\tau_{\text{max}}} \quad \text{for} \quad 0 \leq x \leq \frac{3}{8} \frac{Fc\sigma_{\text{max}}}{lb\tau_{\text{max}}}
\]  
